# Generated at runtime by scripts that resolve BASE_DIR relative to their
# own file location; only backend/src/satcom_core/*.py is a real package,
# so a script accidentally run from the wrong cwd/path in the past has
# regenerated compliance logs and quarantined-model artifacts under
# backend/ instead of the real, referenced top-level compliance/ dir.
# Removed the stray copies once (see git history); ignored so they don't
# quietly get re-tracked.
backend/compliance/
backend/quarantine/
backend/src/compliance/
backend/src/quarantine/
.numba_cache/
numba_cache/

# Developer tools
graphify-out/
.agents/

# Cryptographic key material.
#
# compliance/defense_root_private.pem, defense_root_public.pem, and
# deployment_private.pem were committed to git history (see
# scripts/secure_model_deployer.py and scripts/generate_release_manifest.py)
# -- self-generated Ed25519 demo/bootstrap keys ("Bootstrapping Genesis
# Defense Root Anchor... strictly for testing execution", per that script's
# own comment), not externally-provisioned production credentials, but
# committing ANY key material -- demo or real -- defeats the point of a
# signing scheme: anyone who clones the repo could forge "validly signed"
# artifacts under that identity. Both scripts already auto-generate a fresh
# keypair locally if the files are missing, so untracking is safe and
# sufficient going forward; nothing else in the repo depends on the specific
# committed key. NOTE: the old keypair remains in git history (commits
# a7ba117, 74e4acd) -- treat it as permanently compromised (never use it for
# anything beyond local demo signing) and use `git filter-repo`/BFG if a
# full history purge is ever required; that rewrite was not performed here
# since it changes commit hashes and needs explicit sign-off.
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# LaTeX / build auxiliary artifacts (regenerated from the .tex sources)
*.synctex.gz
*.aux
*.toc
*.out
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
docs/*.log
Proposal/*.log

# Local experimental scratch scripts (do not commit throwaway exploration)
scratch/
tests/scratch_*.py
